From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(telemetry): bring span attribution up to its PR

Match https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11380 (user, runner and
host):

- The host daemon stamps omnigent.host.id as an OTel resource attribute
  before init, so its spans and the runners and harnesses it spawns carry it.
  set_resource_attribute() replaces the Codex env's hand-rolled merge.
- Runner attribution goes through debug_logging.current_runner_id(), which
  falls back to OMNIGENT_RUNNER_ID only in runner and harness processes
  (recorded by configure_process_logging).
- Drop OMNIGENT_OTEL_LOCAL_USER, which the PR does not carry: enduser.id is
  the bound user id as is.
- Document OMNIGENT_OTEL_CAPTURE_USER and cover the new paths with tests.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
